fact WorkItem(id: "WI-996", description: some(value: "UMBRELLA for docs/proposals/059-secondary-entries.md — secondary entries: one scope,\na main entry and secondary ones. 059 is the spec for this work; do NOT re-decide its\nrules in a child ticket. If an implementation cannot meet a rule, AMEND 059 rather\nthan diverging from it.\n\nWHAT 059 SETTLES. A `namespace X` at an address that already has a main entry\n(`sort X` / `enum X` / `entity X`) is a SECONDARY ENTRY to that type's scope — not a\nmodule attached to it. Measured, the visibility is already symmetric in every\ndirection: a secondary entry reads the sort's type parameters, calls its members\nbare, names its variants in a match; the main entry sees the secondary entry's\nmembers and dot-dispatches them on its own receiver. NOTHING IS MISSING IN THE\nWIRING. What is missing is BOUNDS — today two secondary entries declaring one member\nname is silent last-wins, a secondary entry redeclaring a main-entry member silently\nwins, and a second `sort C { … }` body silently reopens a closed ADT.\n\nTHE RULES, and where each lands:\n  R1 a type is defined once ........................ ledger ticket\n  R2 a secondary entry declares members of X ....... NO WORK — measured, already true\n  R3 members and spec claims, never identity ....... classification ticket\n  R4 FILL, never DISPLACE (3 clauses) .............. three tickets\n  R5 §6.3's remedy restated ........................ doc only, spec-sync ticket\n  R6 head binding independent of order ............. WI-980 (exists)\n\nR2 IS DELIVERED BY MEASUREMENT, NOT BY CODE. It is listed so nobody builds it: the\nscope sharing it describes is what the loader already does. Its only follow-up is\nWI-978 — the backing obligation for a `provides` does not reach one declared in a\nsecondary entry, so R3's allowance of spec claims there is unguarded until that lands.\n\nSTILL OPEN AND NOT OWNED HERE: WI-994 (variant exposure is order-dependent),\nWI-995 (an import is scoped to the address, not the file — 059 states the rule,\nthat ticket implements it), WI-895 + WI-980 (both gate 059's NARROW rule for rules\nin a secondary entry; until they close the enforced rule is the blanket ban).\n\nONE DEPENDENCY OUTSIDE THIS REPO'S DELIVERED STATE: 059's R4 clause 2 and its\nspec-claim arbitration both rest on 058 §3.6 (`one_default`, no-displacement), which\nis PROPOSED, not delivered. 059's banner promises every claim is measured against the\nRust loader; that one is not. Resolve before R4 clause 2 lands."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-997", "WI-998", "WI-999", "WI-1000", "WI-1001", "WI-1002", "WI-1003", "WI-978"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Open)
